# Product SKU + name display

Whenever a **CRM product SKU** is shown to users, show the **localized product name** as well.

## Use

- **React UI:** `ProductSkuLabel` from `@/components/product-sku-label`
  - `layout="stack"` — tables, cards (name above, SKU below in mono)
  - `layout="inline"` — compact lists (`Név · SKU`)
  - `href` — optional link to `/inventory/{sku}`
- **Strings / descriptions:** `formatProductSkuLine(name, sku)` or `productDisplayName(names, sku)` from `@crm/lib`
- **Table rows with `ProductTableRow`:** `productNameFromParts(row)` pattern or `name_hu ?? name_en ?? sku`

## Autocomplete / search results

Primary `label` = product name (or SKU if no name). `sublabel` = CRM SKU when distinct. Keep `raw` product on the item so editors can read `sku` reliably.

## Exceptions (SKU alone is OK)

- Hidden form fields (`<input type="hidden" name="sku">`)
- Form inputs where the user **edits** the SKU (`product-form-excel` create flow)
- Category / supplier slug fields (not product CRM SKU)
- Technical logs and import error messages that cite a single identifier

## Do not

- Render bare `{row.sku}` or `font-mono` SKU in tables, links, or detail panels without the name.
- Split name and SKU into distant columns without both visible in the same row context.
